course: dictionary
lesson: 4703
title: Honeydew: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, shows you which meaning the writer wants. Honeydew is a good example.
explain: «Lime trees have heart-shaped leaves; aphids on them drop sweet honeydew.» Here honeydew is a sticky liquid made by insects. The clue is that it drops from aphids on the leaves, not from a plant or a fruit.
explain: «The honeydew melon was cut into pale green slices for the fruit salad.» Here the clues are melon, slices and fruit salad, so honeydew means the fruit. To check, swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Honeydew is a kind of melon with smooth pale skin and sweet pale-green flesh.
fact: Honeydew is also a sweet, sticky liquid made by insects such as aphids.
fact: «Aphids give out a sweet drop called honeydew, ants drink it.»
fact: Ants guard aphids from ladybirds, and some ants stroke aphids to get their honeydew.
fact: Honeydew can make leaves and cars under a tree sticky, as in «a windscreen covered in sticky drops».
exercise: In «aphids on them drop sweet honeydew», what is honeydew? | A pale-green melon for a fruit salad | A kind of lime tree | A spiky grey larva | *A sweet, sticky liquid made by aphids
exercise: «Park a car under a lime tree in July and come back to a windscreen covered in sticky drops.» What makes the windscreen sticky? | *Honeydew dribbled by aphids in the leaves | Summer rain | Sap oozing from the bark | Lime fruit falling from the tree
exercise: «The honeydew melon was cut into pale green slices for the fruit salad.» Which clue tells you honeydew means the fruit? | Sticky drops | The word cut means to sting | Aphids and ladybirds | *Melon, slices and fruit salad
test: «Then ants walk up the stem to stroke the aphids and drink their sweet honeydew.» In this sentence, what is honeydew? | A leaf on the stem | A kind of ladybird | A fruit with pale-green flesh | *A sweet liquid that the aphids give out
test: Why do ants guard aphids? | *To keep them safe from ladybirds, in return for their honeydew | Because aphids are a type of melon | To make the lime tree grow taller | To eat the ladybirds
exam: Jayden has guessed a meaning for honeydew. What should he check to see if his guess is right? | *Whether his meaning still makes sense when swapped into the sentence | Whether the word is longer than the others | Whether he has heard the word before | Whether it sounds like another word he knows
